<title>FINLAND: PTT sees 4.2 pct Finnish 97 growth, slow inflation.</title>
<headline>PTT sees 4.2 pct Finnish 97 growth, slow inflation.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Pellervo Institute of Economic Research (PTT) said on Thursday it had raised its forecast for Finnish 1997 growth in gross domestic product to 4.2 percent from the 2.5 percent forecast last autumn.</p>
<p>Forecasting 3.8 percent growth for 1998, PTT said in a statement that growth would be fuelled by a rapid increase in private consumption, and by strong exports.</p>
<p>&quot;Inflation is no problem although it will pick up speed slightly,&quot; PTT said. It forecast this year's rise in consumer prices at 1.0 percent and saw 1998 inflation at 2.0 percent.  </p>
<p>Key figures in PTT's 1997 spring forecast:</p>
<p>				 1997	1998	1996</p>
<p> GDP			   +4.2	+3.8	+3.3</p>
<p> Imports			 +7	  +6	+4.5</p>
<p> Exports			 +7	  +6	+3.8</p>
<p> Consumption		 +3.5	+2.5	+3.2</p>
<p>   private		   +4.5	  +3	+3.3</p>
<p>   public		    +0.5	+1.0	+2.9</p>
<p> Investment		    +8	+9.5	+5.5</p>
<p>   private		     +8	 +10	+6.7</p>
<p>   public			+8	  +7	+0.1 </p>
<p> CPI			   +1.0	+2.0	+0.6</p>
<p> Unemployment (pct)	14.6	13.7	15.7</p>
<p> C/A (bln markka)	   +20	 +24     +19.2</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, e-mail news@reuters.fi</p>
